    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0151" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.60A/7–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-24T11:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">July</hi> 24, 1945—11 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1132. Department desires that you approach the Chinese Government at your
                    discretion to prevent employment of German technicians. (ReEmbs despatch #32,
                    June 30, 1945<anchor n="77" xml:id="d107-f1"/>). Accepted policy of the United
                    Nations is to keep enemy technicians idle and to prepare for repatriation when
                    possible. We understand desire of Chinese industrialists <pb facs="0152" n="142"
                        xml:id="pg142"/> and authorities in using assistance of German technicians,
                    but in order to achieve a common policy and mutual understanding, such personnel
                    should not be used regardless of how innocent or locally beneficial such
                    services may appear. Other United Nations are cooperating in this policy and it
                    is hoped that Chinese Government will lend its support in making this policy
                    unanimous.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
